## 3. Test touched
None. a#29's first wording ("una via de comunicacion posible") dropped the `feasible-method-only` disclosure
token that src/data/__tests__/guidance-disclosure-parity.test.ts matches with /forma posible|via posible/ for
es. Rather than edit the cross-locale test, the sentence was written as "si existe una via posible de
comunicacion", which is equally natural, still removes the tautology, and keeps the token. All 2770 tests pass
unmodified.

## 4. Reviewer rows I disagreed with / could not apply as written
D1 a#1 ("visibilidad" -> "insercion publicitaria"). The English canonical notice is "it does not promise search
   ranking, endorsement, AI recommendation, or guaranteed visibility" - "insercion publicitaria" (advertising
   placement) is a different claim. Applied the rest of the row and wrote "visibilidad garantizada".
D2 b#41 (018: renumber 5/7/8 as 5/6/7). NOT APPLIED. The Korean source (src/content/columns/018, headings
   1,2,3,4,5,7,8) and the English source have the same gap. Renumbering the Spanish would delete the numeral
   8 that the source carries, and check-column-translation's `numbers` check treats a missing source figure as
   FAIL. This is a source-side defect and needs a decision on ko/en first.
D3 b#20 ("hasta 1 vez el importe" -> "hasta el importe"). Dropping the numeral removes a figure the checker
   counts, and the sentence is a 5 / 3 / 1 series ("hasta 5 veces ... hasta 3 veces ... hasta 1 vez").
   Written as "hasta una vez el importe del dano real".
D4 a#30 (bio "TWD 1.57M" -> "1,57 millones de TWD"). GUIDANCE_BIO_PRESERVED_TERMS + guidance-team-bios.test.ts
   require "TWD 1.57M" byte-identical in every locale bio, and that rule is cross-locale, not an es string.
   Kept the token and appended the Spanish reading: "TWD 1.57M (1,57 millones de dolares taiwaneses)".
D5 b#11 scope. 戶籍 as a record is now "registro de domicilio (戶籍)" everywhere (007, 016, guidance; 017
   already had it). But 戶政機關 / 戶政事務所 (the office where a divorce is registered) and 戶籍法 keep
   "oficina del registro civil (戶政機關)" / "Ley del registro civil (戶籍法)": es-a explicitly approved that
   rendering, and "registro civil" is the Spanish institution a reader maps a divorce registration to.
D6 a#44 sec.7 of 007 ("No son el mismo derecho."). Left unchanged: unlike "No." / "No siempre.", this opener
   already states a proposition that stands on its own.
D7 a#18 / the 005 percent-encoded Korean Wix href. Skipped per ACCEPTED-es; additionally the English source
   carries the identical href, so changing it would break the checker's `links` parity.

